From 6ecddcf10ae8246015d18d224a13261f0cdfdd57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:37:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] grate: skip draws while no vertex or fragment shader is bound

grate_create_vs_state() and grate_create_fs_state() return NULL for a
program they cannot compile, so the state tracker binds nothing, and the
next draw read context->fshader->info or context->vshader->blob through a
NULL pointer.

Firefox (WebRender) tripped over this: a WebRender fragment shader that was
too large for the register budget ("no free register for the SFU op")
failed to compile, and the compositor died with a SIGSEGV on its next draw.
That looked like an unexplained "AbnormalShutdown" with no message.

Skip the draw instead. The affected primitives are missing from the
picture, which is better than losing the process.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
index c582794521b..eb80d202d90 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
@@ -365,6 +365,11 @@ grate_draw_vbo(struct pipe_context *pcontext,
    if (!indirect && (!draws[0].count || !info->instance_count))
       return;
 
+   /* A shader that failed to compile is never created, so the state tracker
+    * binds none. Skip the draw instead of dereferencing it. */
+   if (!context->vshader || !context->fshader)
+      return;
+
    if (context->blend_dual && !context->dual_pass) {
       grate_draw_dual(pcontext, info, drawid_offset, indirect, draws,
                       num_draws);
